<title>CHINA: China 1996 cotton harvest seen down 1.0 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>China 1996 cotton harvest seen down 1.0 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's cotton harvest is expected to plummet to around 3.5 million tonnes in 1996, a drop of more than 1.0 million tonnes compared with last year, the official Xinhua news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Output is expected to tumble due to a 534,000 hectare reduction in the area under cotton, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>Lack of price incentives and rising domestic cotton stocks have led many farmers to switch to other crops, analysts have said.</p>
<p>Earlier official forecasts predicted China's cotton output would be 3.8 million tonnes this year.</p>
</text>
